After thinking about this for a bit, perhaps the holidays should be
associated with the Player's class rather than the player (except
tourists).  Since the classes one can play in NetHack all have roots in
different nations, why not apply the holidays according to the class?

For example, Valkyrie are based on the Norse mythos.  Perhaps using
holidays significant to the Norse mythos and history would suffice.
Thus the holidays available would be Easter, Yule, Mabon, Winternights
and Litha (however three are equinox or solstice based excluding
Winternights which is New Years).

Samurai is based on the Japanese class system.  Therefore, the holidays
that occur during Golden Week can be applied where appropriate.

As for tourists, tourists can pick their nationality at player creation
time.  Thus, the holiday will apply to either the character's or the
player's nationality.

I know that would take a bit of work to implement but it is an
interesting concept.



